## Key Concepts

- API Management as secure, centralized ingress boundary
- Event Hubs for reliable, scalable ingestion
- Functions for idempotent, serverless processing
- Cosmos DB (SQL API) with tenantId partitioning and TTL for retention
- Power BI DirectQuery for near-real-time dashboards
- Azure AD RBAC for per-tenant isolation
- Key Vault-backed BYOK and encryption-at-rest
- Cost controls: autoscale, reserved capacity, budgets

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example: pseudocode for a Function that writes to Cosmos DB
const { CosmosClient } = require('@azure/cosmos');
const client = new CosmosClient(process.env.COSMOS_ENDPOINT, process.env.COSMOS_KEY);
async function handleEvent(event) {
  const tenantId = event.tenantId;
  const item = { id: event.id, tenantId, ...event.payload, ts: Date.now() };
  await client.database('TenantDb').container('Events').items.upsert(item);
}
```

